Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design secure, scalable data pipelines for finance with strong privacy controls and tenancy separation. Covers data privacy (DLP, CMEK), access control (IAM conditions), reliability (idempotent writes, backoff), and cross-region considerations for data residency. Also probes testing, rollout, and rollback strategies.

Key Concepts

- DLP and PII tokenization
- CMEK and envelope encryption
- IAM Conditions and least privilege
- Per-tenant partitioning in BigQuery
- Dataflow streaming guarantees and backpressure
- Cross-region replication and data residency
- Idempotency with insertId and replay handling
- Observability and audit trails with Cloud Audit Logs

